note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note seed/host/realset/realset.om: fixture for realset (keyword 236), program mode. Run by the OM-2
note conductor through seed/host/realset/realset.cases from the repository root, as a user without
note CAP_SYS_TIME: the fixture never changes the host clock. Kernel truth: Linux clock_settime checks
note the timespec (timespec64_valid_settod: tv_nsec below 1e9, tv_sec below TIME_SETTOD_SEC_MAX =
note KTIME_SEC_MAX - 30*365*86400 = 8277292036) before the capability check, so an unprivileged caller
note sees -22 (EINVAL) for an invalid timespec and -1 (EPERM) for a valid one. That makes the exact
note seconds/nanoseconds split, the clock id and the syscall number observable without privilege.
note Checks (parent exit = number of the first failed check, 0 when all hold):
note 1 realset of the current realns returns -1 (EPERM): a valid REALTIME timespec reached the
note   capability check (a wrong clock id gives -22, clock_gettime in place of clock_settime gives 0).
note 2 realset 9223372036854775807 (2^63-1 ns, tv_sec 9223372036) returns -22.
note 3 realset 8277292035999999999 (tv_sec 8277292035, tv_nsec 999999999, the last valid instant)
note   returns -1: seconds = ns / 1e9 and nanoseconds = ns mod 1e9, in that order.
note 4 realset 8277292036000000000 (tv_sec 8277292036, the first invalid second) returns -22.
note 5 a negative ns traps 3 in a forked child (exit 103) before any kernel call.
note 6 realset 0 (the epoch, valid) returns -1.
note 7 the realtime clock did not jump: realns after the checks is within 10 s of realns before.
note A process running with euid 0 would change the clock, so the fixture refuses to run (exit 90).
om2
global status uchar 4

fn reap pid long to ulong
r = waitpid int pid status 0 len status 0
if ne r pid
ret 1000
end
if ne get status 0 0
ret add 2000 ulong and get status 0 127
end
ret ulong get status 1
end

note A forked child calls realset with ns; returns the child's exit (103 is trap 3).
fn trapkid ns long to ulong
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
ret 1001
end
if eq pid 0
r = realset ns
exit 98
end
ret reap pid
end

fn main to int
if eq geteuid 0
ret 90
end
t0 = realns
if lt t0 0
ret 91
end
r = realset t0
if ne r neg long 1
ret 1
end
r = realset 9223372036854775807
if ne r neg long 22
ret 2
end
r = realset 8277292035999999999
if ne r neg long 1
ret 3
end
r = realset 8277292036000000000
if ne r neg long 22
ret 4
end
if ne trapkid neg long 1 103
ret 5
end
r = realset long 0
if ne r neg long 1
ret 6
end
t1 = realns
if or lt t1 t0 gt sub t1 t0 10000000000
ret 7
end
ret 0
end
